  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "d4aef09ebf91140a11a6bb2828501dfc87ecd274",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1754752298,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> I'm not entirely sure if it is safe to modify the definition of `WS_DLL_PUBLIC` function `register_all_tap_listeners` in this way\n\nI don't know of anything that would cause API or ABI breakage if you add a `const` qualifier to an argument or to the target of a pointer argument; software that depends on a routine that's *not* required to modify what an argument points to modifying it nevertheless isn't going to work in any case.\n\n(Not that we have strong API or ABI guarantees between major releases.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
